{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And Canaan begot Tzidon.</b> He had eleven sons, and in conclusion it says 'afterward the families of the Canaanite were spread abroad.' This teaches you that one became two, making twelve — like Joseph, who was split into two tribes. Concerning this it is said, 'He set the borders of the peoples according to the number of the children of Israel' (Deut. 32:8): twelve sons of Canaan were given to twelve tribes. And Moses our teacher called them seven: the six that were prominent he called by name separately, and the rest he included under the name of their father, the Canaanite — because his sons honored Abraham our father in the acquisition of the cave of Machpelah."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {0 "The phrase משפחות הכנעני is cited from Gen. 10:18; בנ״י/שי״ב/י״‎ב resolved as בני ישראל/שנים עשר/שנים עשר."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:03:48.262474963Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}